crates.io package through [patch.crates-io] in zest_native's Cargo.toml. What came from the crate
stays under its licence; our change follows this folder's licence too (MIT or Apache-2.0).

What changed against 0.12.0, and nothing else:

  - src/connection.rs: an Auto-Detect Request that comes after the connect-time phase is answered,
    and anything else on the message channel is passed over, in every phase that waits on the
    I/O channel. A Windows Server 2022 RD Session Host with RDS licensing sends one in the middle
    of the licensing exchange and again before the Demand Active; each later phase handed it to
    its own decoder, and the licensing header's "invalid security header flags" ended the
    connection before the session opened (IronRDP issue #1629). Upstream IronRDP's own fix,
    905c28b3a4 (#2128), line for line.
  - The package's Cargo.toml.orig, Cargo.lock and .cargo_vcs_info.json are left out: they are
    not used by a build from a path.
  - Long dashes in src/lib.rs are plain hyphens: this repository keeps none. No code changed by it.

When IronRDP releases the fix, this folder goes and the crate comes from crates.io again.
